<title>BAHRAIN: Bahraini-U.S. joint venture wins $14.3 mln platform deal.</title>
<headline>Bahraini-U.S. joint venture wins $14.3 mln platform deal.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A United States-Bahraini joint venture has won a $14.3 million contract to build an offshore jack-up barge in the Gulf Arab state, the Gulf Daily News said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said international oil company Sedco Forex awarded the contract to TDI Nass, a joint venture between Abdullah Ahmed Nass Group and the U.S. firm Texas Drydock Incorporated (TDI).</p>
<p>The daily said the floating platform will be used to carry out repair and maintenance work on offshore oil rigs.</p>
<p>Work is expected to start in December and take 18 months to complete.</p>
</text>
